<figcaption>Where today's update lands. The agent and capacity stories are the ones to plan around.</figcaption>
</figure>

<section class="block">
<h2>1. Google releases Gemini 4 Carbon to cyber defenders first</h2>
<p>Google announced Gemini 4 Carbon on 28 October as its next frontier model, with a focus on cybersecurity and long-running engineering tasks<sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-1">1</a></sup><sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-2">2</a></sup>. Access starts with a small group of cyber defenders, widening to trusted partners through a dedicated programme, with no date yet for general developers; the benchmark results quoted are Google's own<sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-3">3</a></sup>.</p>
<p><strong>CTO take:</strong> staged, defender-first releases are becoming the norm for models with serious offensive potential. Expect the same capability to reach attackers eventually, so shorten patch cycles now, as this week's <a href="/case-studies/legacy-php-estate-security-modernisation/">PHP2Shell response</a> showed. Security teams should also ask their vendors whether they are in these early-access programmes.</p>
</section>

<section class="block">
<h2>2. Azure grows 48% and demand still exceeds supply</h2>
<p>Microsoft's quarterly results showed Azure revenue up 48%, ahead of estimates, with capital spending of $45.2 billion, below its own projection, which the company attributed to delivery timing rather than a change of plan<sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-4">4</a></sup>. Fortune reports that the CFO said demand still exceeds supply<sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-5">5</a></sup>.</p>
<p><strong>CTO take:</strong> constrained AI capacity is a planning input, not a headline. If you depend on GPU or managed model capacity in a specific region, reserve it early, keep at least one alternative provider or model ready, and track <a href="/insights/focus-finops-ai-cost-allocation/">AI cost allocation</a> so you know which workloads deserve the capacity you do get.</p>
</section>

<section class="block">
<h2>3. Jio Platforms opens 21% up after India's largest IPO</h2>
<p>Jio Platforms began trading on 28 October, with shares up more than 21% on debut after a record IPO; Reliance remains the majority owner, with Meta and Google affiliates also holding stakes<sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-6">6</a></sup>.</p>
<p><strong>CTO take:</strong> a listed, heavily capitalised Jio raises the bar for digital infrastructure and AI services in India. For companies building there, expect more competition for engineering talent and more local cloud and AI options. Data-protection preparation for the DPDP Rules matters more as scale grows; see <a href="/case-studies/india-dpdp-consent-platform-lending/">a DPDP-ready consent platform</a> and <a href="/fractional-cto-india/">fractional CTO in India</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="block">
<h2>4. Meta's Muse agent launches in Singapore with local partners</h2>
<p>Meta made its personal AI agent, Muse, available in Singapore, with partners including Shopee and Grab<sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-7">7</a></sup><sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-8">8</a></sup>. On Grab, it can build a basket for a meal or essentials and wait for the user's approval before ordering; Meta says Muse asks for approval before sensitive steps such as purchases or sending email<sup class="cite"><a href="#ref-8">8</a></sup>.</p>
<p><strong>CTO take:</strong> customers will increasingly arrive through agents rather than your app. If you run commerce, travel or services in Southeast Asia, check that your catalogue, pricing and booking APIs are machine-readable and that approval and refund flows work when an agent is acting for a person. See <a href="/insights/structured-data-for-ai-search/">structured data for AI search</a> and <a href="/fractional-cto-singapore/">fractional CTO in Singapore</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="block">
<h2>What I'd do this week</h2>
<ul>
<li>Ask security vendors whether they have early access to cyber-focused models, and shorten patch timelines regardless.</li>
<li>Review AI and GPU capacity commitments by region, and name a fallback provider or model.</li>
<li>Test your public APIs and product data from an agent's point of view: can it find, compare and book without scraping?</li>
<li>Keep DPDP readiness on the plan if you operate in India.</li>
</ul>
<p>Working across these markets? See <a href="/regions/">where I work</a>, or <a href="/#assess">analyse your challenge</a> and bring the result to a call.</p>
</section>
